Kind: ablation
Issue: #799
Over: 799-widen-dispatch.patch
Takes out: the order -- state is written first, as i386's compiler wrote it at two sites of three, with the 200 us of the widen before next_thread.  An idle processor that leaves its wait in that window, or an interrupt on it in thread_setrun(), finds DISPATCHING and nothing to run.
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: is DISPATCHING with no next_thread

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
index 5a02d55e..add7a8ec 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
@@ -2982,10 +2982,10 @@ urmach_processor_dispatch(
 	processor_t	processor,
 	thread_t	th)
 {
-	processor->next_thread = th;
+	processor->state = PROCESSOR_DISPATCHING;
 	urmach_rcu_barrier();
 	delay(200);
-	processor->state = PROCESSOR_DISPATCHING;
+	processor->next_thread = th;
 }
 
